<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Noshout and Notell</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>noshout &lt;player&gt;                 (200: for 30 minutes)
noshout &lt;player&gt; 25 min          (for as long as you say)
noshout &lt;player&gt; 1 hour
notell &lt;player&gt;                  (240)
</pre>
<p><b>noshout</b> gives a player "a sore throat": they can't shout until it 
wears off, or until you noshout them again, which lifts it. Their 
channels, says and tells still work. Use it when a player spams or abuses 
shout. Players see how long they have left with noshouted (see 
<a cmd='#'>Help Noshout</a>). New Player Guides may noshout players of level 20 and 
below.
</p><p><b>notell</b> takes away a player's tells ("Your telepathic ability fades 
away!") until you notell them again ("You regain your telepathic 
ability."); there is no time limit. Use it on a player who harasses 
someone with tells. Who did it, and when, is noted on the player.
</p><p>Both work on players anywhere in the game, but not on players of your 
level or higher. Both are logged.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Noshout</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Freeze</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Ignore</a>
</pre>




</div>